WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 4.2 · People, Culture & Volunteers
Recruitment and fair selection

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Your first role sets the standard: recruit fairly, beyond friends and contacts, from day one.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:25.541
Recruitment is how you find and choose the people who will join you. Fair selection means judging every candidate against the same criteria, agreed before you read any application.

4
00:00:25.941 --> 00:00:26.541
Four steps to fair selection

5
00:00:26.541 --> 00:00:37.870
A clear advert: Purpose, main tasks, essential criteria, pay and how to apply, in plain language. For example: The traineeship advert drops exam requirements: reliability and willingness to learn matter more.

6
00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:48.830
A wide search: Advertise where the people you want actually look, beyond friends and contacts. For example: The bakery shares the traineeship through the youth centre and on local radio.

7
00:00:48.830 --> 00:01:00.530
Fair assessment: Same questions, a scoring guide, at least two people deciding and reasons noted. For example: Two founders score each bakery candidate on a short practical bake, then compare notes.

8
00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:13.430
Safer recruitment: Identity checks, references and safeguarding questions when the role involves children or vulnerable adults. For example: The bakery checks references for every mentor before they work with 17-year-old trainees.

9
00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:14.430
Why it matters

10
00:01:14.430 --> 00:01:20.104
1. Your first role sets the standard for every one after it.

11
00:01:20.104 --> 00:01:26.519
2. A wider search stops you building a team that only looks like you.

12
00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:32.822
3. Written reasons protect you if a decision is questioned later.

13
00:01:33.222 --> 00:01:33.822
What it builds on

14
00:01:33.822 --> 00:01:38.756
1. Your role cards from Module 3 become the adverts.

15
00:01:38.756 --> 00:01:43.319
2. Your contracts and onboarding, next in this module.

16
00:01:43.319 --> 00:01:49.252
3. Your data protection rules: how you keep applicants' records.

17
00:01:49.652 --> 00:01:50.252
What to avoid

18
00:01:50.252 --> 00:01:53.704
Asking only friends and contacts.

19
00:01:53.704 --> 00:01:59.007
Requirements that exclude people without good reason, like unneeded degrees.

20
00:01:59.007 --> 00:02:04.570
Skipping safeguarding checks because “we already know them”.

21
00:02:05.170 --> 00:02:06.970
You design the recruitment process for your first or next role.

22
00:02:06.970 --> 00:02:10.970
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

23
00:02:12.470 --> 00:02:15.570
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
